    "reviewed_findings": [
      "All 94 fixed-scope file hashes match the current files using Windows extended-length paths for deep snapshots.",
      "Reviewed the six shared formal pages and all three implementation pages. The actual bindings are exactly P1/M1 Kickback Lorenz Mk V, P2/M2 Rumbler Lorenz Mk VI, and P3/M3 Thugshot Lorenz Mk VII; weapon ids, mark ids, trait ids, RAW UI names, and template import/append records match the three-item UI receipt and current global map.",
      "The player guide distinguishes melee impact from damage, explains first cache update, held/equip/switch behavior, finite HitMass budget and breed abort limits, and excludes P2 projectile/explosion from HitMass reduction. Both examples state their assumptions and limit results to intermediate stagger power or hit-mass budget.",
      "I–IV values are 0.10/0.15/0.20/0.25 and all three wrappers/traits agree. Formatter reconstruction uses the matching English/zh-TW RAW key/hash and + percentage prefix; it does not promise final stagger strength or time.",
      "The localization comparison table has ten rows, five cells in each row, and correctly orders RAW text, source behavior with script paths/methods/ranges, comparison result, and reason. Its rows exactly match both canonical config and extension-draft rules.",
      "The icon receipt identifies weapon_trait_133 separately from its attachment URL; README and current map use that same attachment. The three weapon reverse indexes link back to the Pierce entry.",
      "The row-38 entry in Pierce LOCALIZATION_COMPARISON.md is the held/equip/cache rule; the prior Combatblade concern was a mistaken cross-task recollection and does not occur anywhere in Pierce scope."
